# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Pages serves /assets/* with `max-age=14400` — four hours. HTML is revalidated
# on every request, so a deploy that renames a CSS class ships new HTML to browsers that are still
# holding the OLD stylesheet for up to four hours. The element then has a class nothing styles, and it
# renders as an invisible empty div.
#
# That is exactly what happened when `.hero` became `.portrait`: the photograph of Dan vanished from
# the masthead for anyone who had loaded the site earlier that day, while a fresh browser saw it fine
# — which is the worst kind of bug, because it looks correct to whoever just deployed it.
#
# The stylesheet is ~10 KB and is the one file that MUST stay in lockstep with the HTML, so it
# revalidates every time. A 304 costs a round trip and no bytes. Images keep the long cache: their
# URLs change when their content does.
/assets/site.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
